{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773306045,"nonce":"+b2M7L2sejt3sifxsl9Y0FIeiyM=","title":"Fix review container name collision with coder container","message":"When the watcher auto-resumes an orphaned review session, it launches a container that collides with the coder container name.\n\nThe review session ID is `review-\u003csid\u003e`, but launch.py produces `nightshift-\u003csid\u003e` as the container name for both coder and reviewer.\n\nError:\n```\ndocker: Error response from daemon: Conflict. The container name \"/nightshift-c4c24c77afd6\" is already in use\n```\n\n## Fix needed\n\nIn `host/docker_cmd.py` (builds the docker run command), ensure the container name matches the session ID. Since review sessions have IDs like `review-\u003csid\u003e`, the container name should be `nightshift-review-\u003csid\u003e`.\n\nCheck `host/docker_cmd.py:build_docker_cmd()` and `host/launch.py` for where container_name is constructed. The session_name/short_id already includes the `review-` prefix — make sure it flows through to the `--name` flag.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Review containers named `nightshift-review-\u003csid\u003e`, coder containers named `nightshift-\u003csid\u003e`\n- [ ] No container name collisions during concurrent coder + reviewer runs\n- [ ] Tests covering both naming patterns\n\nREQ-009","files":null}]}